218	<h3><span class="num">Rule 4 &middot; SKILL.md, “Talking to the curator”, a new last bullet under “While the curator reads turn by turn” &middot; redrafted &middot; waits for your read</span>Small turns for page comments</h3>
219	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">New text: a new bullet</span>
220	<ul><li>While the curator comments on a page, the page keeps the comments, so each comment's turn stays small: “.” in chat, and the point kept in your context. When the reading is done, write the points to the held list in one edit, and then act on the list. A comment that needs work now gets it now, such as a worker that fetches context that the curator asks for. A comment that opens a discussion gets its answer on its thread.</li></ul>
221	</div></div>
222	<details class="prior"><summary>Version 4's text (tap to open)</summary><div>
223	<ul><li>When the curator comments on a page, the page's threads hold the points. <span class="cut">Reply on each thread with its held line and “holding”,</span> reply “.” in chat, and write the held lines of the whole reading in one edit and one commit when the reading is done.</li></ul>
224	</div></details>
225	<div class="note"><p><strong>What it changes and why.</strong> Today the skill has no rule for a page's comments, and on 29 October the coordinator wrote each point three times and committed the held list after each comment. With this bullet, a comment costs a “.” in chat, the held list gets one edit when you finish, and then the coordinator acts on the list. “Holding” on each thread goes, and the bullet names the two cases that get an answer at once: work that a comment needs now, and a discussion that you open.</p></div>
